    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">All studies included on this page are generator interconnection studies.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">We use RSGM for the calculation of excess deferred taxes to customers. The deferred taxes associated with public utility plant property will be amortized over a period ranging from 3 to 71 years and we amortize the excess deferred taxes associated with other types of deferred taxes that are not related to public utility property over a period of 51-years.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">All schedules use MISO as billing agent.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Network load is populated on Schedule 9 on page 400. No information is provided in column (h) for billing demand, since these pages report Transmission Revenue dollars by schedule and demand information is not readily available (other than Schedule 9) and is maintained by MISO.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The amounts reported in column (d) represent the peak network loads. Columns (b) and (c) are not filled out since it is not applicable to our business as we are a transmission only company and do not report or use Monthly Energy amounts nor Monthly Sale or Resale values for our business.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">No information is reported in columns (e) &#8211; (j) as such information is maintained by MISO as the billing agent and not readily available. However, network load is reported in column (b).</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents issuance of long-term debt of $175,000,000 and borrowings under the revolving credit agreement of $124,000,000.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents borrowings under the revolving credit agreement.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents repayments of the revolving credit agreement.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents repayments of the revolving credit agreement.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-19" id="fn-19" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents cash balance in accounts 131 and 136.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-20" id="fn-20" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Line 12, column (b) includes $0 of unbilled revenues</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-21" id="fn-21" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Line 12, column (d) includes 0 MWH relating to unbilled revenues</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">In compliance with Schedule 50 Order approved on March 19, 2020 under the Federal Regulatory Commission docket number ER20-170, ITC Midwest invoices the generators for annual operations and maintenance costs associated with Transmission Owner&#8217;s Interconnection Facilities calculated for actual year 2024, pursuant to Article 10, Section 10.5 of their Generator Interconnection Agreement.</link:footnote>
